<title>UK: EMI rises as talk of MCA bid resurfaces.</title>
<headline>EMI rises as talk of MCA bid resurfaces.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in music publisher EMI Group Plc rose on Monday as a Sunday newspaper report repeated rumours of a possible takeover bid by MCA Music Entertainment Group, a unit of Seagram Co Ltd.</p>
<p>At 1140 GMT, EMI shares were up 7-1/2p at 13.80 stg.</p>
<p>The Sunday Business newspaper said MCA was considering a 6.6 billion stg hostile bid for EMI. With the sale of surplus assets, MCA would be able to raise two billion stg in cash for the bid and would borrow the rest, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>-- Brian Killen, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7972</p>
